    {
      "filename": "Day 2- Liverpool Cathedral (8385405728).jpg",
      "title": "File:Day 2- Liverpool Cathedral (8385405728).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5a/Day_2-_Liverpool_Cathedral_%288385405728%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Day_2-_Liverpool_Cathedral_(8385405728).jpg",
      "width": 3249,
      "height": 4889,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "Takashi Hososhima from Tokyo, Japan",
      "description": "Liverpool Cathedral is definitely the most impressive and breathtaking cathedral during my trip to the UK.(St Paul's Cathedral in London is also great, but photography is not permitted inside)\nTrip photography tend to end up with a lot of snap shots and less great shots. But I'm sure this is the one of the best shots of my photos of the trip. I'd like say a big thank you to tofu_catgirl and K who take me to the cathedral.\nIf you are interested, you can view original size to find out people and get an idea how huge this cathedral is, and how tiny people are.\nリバプール大聖堂は今回の英国旅行の中で、間違いなく最も立派で最も素晴らしい大聖堂でした。（ロンドンにあるセント・ポール大聖堂も素晴らしいのですが中では写真撮影禁止なのが残念）\n旅行の写真はスナップショット写真が多くなり、これはすごいと思うような写真は少なくなりがちですが、これは結構自信作です。ここに連れて行ってくれたtofu_catgirlさんとKさんに感謝感激です。\nもし興味があったらOriginalサイズでこの写真を見てみてください。ものすごく小さく人が写っています。いかにこの大聖堂が大きいか、いかに人が小さいかがよくわかります。\n\n[ Nikon D4, Nikon AF-S NIKKOR 16-35mm f/4G ED VR, 16mm, f/4.0, 1/20sec, ISO2500, Lightroom 4.3 ]",
      "dateCreated": "2012-12-31 02:01",
